---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Prose from "@/components/Prose.astro";
import { SITE, u } from "@/site";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description={`What ${SITE.name} collects about readers: no cookies, no accounts, and cookieless visit counts from self-hosted analytics.`} path="/privacy/">
  <Prose kicker="Privacy" title="Privacy">
    <p>{SITE.name} is a static website. It has no accounts, no sign-up forms, no comments, no newsletter and no advertising. It does not set cookies, does not run advertising or third-party tracking scripts, and counts visits with a small self-hosted analytics script that keeps no personal data. This page explains each way information about a visit can reach someone, and what we do about it.</p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is served by GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub receives standard request information such as your IP address, browser and the page requested, and may keep it for security and operations. That processing is covered by the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>. {SITE.name} does not receive or store these logs.</p>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>To know which stories are read and where readers come from, the site counts visits with <a href="https://umami.is" rel="noopener">Umami</a>, an open-source analytics tool we run on our own server, loaded from stats.theinjection.dev. Nothing is sent to Google or any other analytics company, and the data is not shared or sold.</p>
    <p>For each page view it records the page, the site you came from (the referrer), your browser, operating system, device type, screen size and language, and an approximate location (country, region and city) looked up from your IP address. It also counts a few clicks: links to other sites (the destination's domain only), the Share, Ask AI and Copy link buttons, the feed filters, video plays and links to the RSS, JSON and text files. What you type in the search box is never sent.</p>
    <p>It sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser. Your IP address is not stored: it is combined with your browser details into a one-way hash so repeat visits can be counted, and that hash changes every month. If your browser sends Do Not Track, the script sends nothing. Blocking stats.theinjection.dev also turns it off; the site works the same either way.</p>
    <h2>Images from sources</h2>
    <p>Some story covers are the original publisher's own preview image, loaded directly from that publisher's server. When your browser loads one, that server sees your IP address. We ask browsers not to send the page you came from (no referrer). Stories without a source image use a cover generated on this site, which loads nothing from third parties.</p>
    <h2>Videos</h2>
    <p>Talk stories show a video cover with a play button. Nothing loads from YouTube until you press play. When you do, the player loads from youtube-nocookie.com, Google's privacy-enhanced embed, and Google's privacy policy applies to that player. You can also open the video on YouTube instead.</p>
    <h2>Fonts and scripts</h2>
    <p>Fonts are hosted on this site, not on a font service. Apart from the analytics script above, the small scripts on the page (filters, the countdown, the exposure strips) run only in your browser and send nothing anywhere.</p>
    <h2>Links out</h2>
    <p>Every story links to its sources. Those sites have their own privacy policies, which apply once you leave {SITE.name}.</p>
    <h2>Share and Ask AI buttons</h2>
    <p>The Share links (X, Bluesky, LinkedIn, Reddit, Hacker News, email) and the Ask AI links (ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Grok) are plain links. Nothing loads from those services until you click one; then it opens the other site with the page's title and address filled in. Copy link uses your browser's clipboard. The analytics above count which of these buttons was clicked, and nothing else about it.</p>
    <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
    <p>If what we collect changes, this page will say so before it happens. Questions about privacy can go through the <a href={u("/contact/")}>contact page</a>.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated October 9, 2026.</p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
